## Show Again After Dismissal

The **Show Again After Dismissal** setting determines whether a nudge can appear again after a customer dismisses it.

The interface displays the following description:

> Once dismissed, won't show again

Select the appropriate option from the dropdown to configure this behaviour.

## Nudge Interaction Limit

The **Nudge Interaction Limit** section allows you to set a threshold for user interactions, after which the nudge stops appearing.

### Configure the Interaction Limit

Under **Nudge Interaction Limit**, select the required attribute from the **Attribute** dropdown.

The available attributes shown in the interface are:

| Attribute | Description |
|---|---|
| **Impression Count** | Represents the number of times the nudge has been displayed to the user. |
| **CTR Count** | Represents the number of click-through interactions associated with the nudge. |

Select the relevant attribute to configure the interaction limit.

### Add More Conditions

Select **Add more** to add another interaction-limit condition.

Use the delete icon to remove a condition that is no longer required.

## What's Next?

After configuring the required interaction settings, select **Continue** to proceed to the **Communication** step.

